EN:
Have you ever heard the phrase,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
{{TAG:0003:0017:}}"Rain falls on good peeps and bad"?{{TAG:0000:0004:}}{{TAG:0003:0000:}}I don't know what it means,{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} but it
seems like a good slogan for anyone
who makes umbrellas.{{TAG:0003:0025:}}

ES:
¿Has oído alguna vez la frase{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
{{TAG:0003:0017:}}"A quien madruga,{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
buena lluvia le cobija"?
{{TAG:0003:0000:}}No sé muy bien qué significa,{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}} 
pero parece sacada de un anuncio
de paraguas.{{TAG:0003:0025:}}

IT:
Hai mai sentito il proverbio{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
{{TAG:0003:0017:}}"La pioggia bagna tutti, belli
e brutti"?{{TAG:0000:0004:}}{{TAG:0003:0000:}}Non ho mai capito bene cosa
significhi,{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} ma potrebbe essere un
buono slogan per un ombrellificio.{{TAG:0003:0025:}}

EN:
{{TAG:0003:001B:}}I've just about had it with this rain.{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
I just wanna take each drop and
punch it in its rainy nose!

ES:
{{TAG:0003:001B:}}Esta dichosa lluvia es insoportable.{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
Además, con la suerte que tengo,
seguro que me voy a casa y para.

IT:
{{TAG:0003:001B:}}Non ne posso più di questa pioggia.{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
Ora prendo ogni singola goccia
e la rimando indietro a calci!

DE:
Mann, ist der Regen lästig.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
{{TAG:0003:001C:}}Ich würd am liebsten jedem Tropfen
einzeln auf die Nase hauen, {{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}grrr!
